## V5 contract

Author:

- canonical domain/reference TTL under `model/ontologies/`;
- source-vocabulary TTL under `integration/sources/`;
- one closed `EntityBinding` per source relation or contracted dbt model under
  `integration/bindings/`;
- optional ordinary contracted dbt SQL/YAML under `integration/transforms/dbt/models/`;
- optional Gold/MDM policy TTL under `model/extensions/`.

Do not add claims, preparation or Silver-extension authority, lifecycle/readiness state,
release evidence, or generated files as authored inputs.

## Compile

```bash
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --check
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --explain --format json
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --emit output/medallion/dbt
```

The adapter is selected in `kairos.yaml` (`fabric` or `databricks`). Every invocation
builds one immutable `CompilePlan`; check and explain do not write.

## Ontology conventions

- One domain per lowercase, hyphenated `.ttl` file.
- Every ontology declares `owl:Ontology`, `rdfs:label`, and `owl:versionInfo`.
- Classes use PascalCase; properties use camelCase.
- Keep `_master.ttl` imports current.
- Keep samples synthetic and free of personal or proprietary data.

V5 is a clean break. Rebuild v4 hubs from this scaffold; no compatibility or conversion
command is provided.
